WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.567
I'm here with the one-and-only
Taylor Swift!

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:08.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.367
Last time you were here,

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:12.667
we talked about your short film
"All Too Well."

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:13.934
It was about to come out.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.033
And then it went on
to win three VMAs,

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.801
including Video of the Year.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:21.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:23.267
Do you think you'll direct
all of your videos

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.300
from here on forward?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.701
-I really love doing it.
-You're great at it.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.000
-Thank you so much.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.100
-Writing them
and then directing them --

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.400
that's kind of the way
that it works in my head.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.434
If I write it,
then I can shot-list it

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:38.868
and I can storyboard it
and I know how to shoot it.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.167
So it's -- They kind of
go hand in hand.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.467
-Yeah.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.868
-If someone else wrote
the concept or the treatment

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:44.968
or the manuscript or whatever,

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:48.100
I don't think
I would love it as much.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.334
But it's the thing
that goes hand in hand,

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.467
the writing and directing.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:54.567
-"Anti-Hero,"
the -- It's hilarious.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:55.634
It's fantastic.
-Thank you!

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:58.033
-I love it. It's so good.
-Thank you.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.968
-My favorite --
Besides some of the casting,

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.133
my favorite is
when you're, like,

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.901
I feel like a
giant's coming in and, like,

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.067
kind of ruining the party
and coming in and not --

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.567
And you sneak in and you're
a giant at this dinner party.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:11.701
And they're all
freaking out, screaming.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:12.868
-Yeah.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.000
-But then you eat --
-Too big to hang out.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.300
-But then -- Yeah.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.267
But then you eat some of
the food with this tiny fork.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.667
-Yeah. It was really --
It was such a blast,

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:23.067
because we had -- We shot that
in two-sized rooms, right?

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.100
Like, one of the rooms had

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.501
our actors who were at
the dinner party,

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.567
and it was a normal-sized room.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:34.167
And they had to act with,
like, a laser pen.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:38.200
And I'd just be, like, "And
a monster's coming in the room.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.634
Follow the laser pen.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.734
It's a scary monster."
-And that's you, yeah.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.801
-And then we had
a teeny, tiny little room

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.834
with a teeny, tiny table.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.000
We just had the most amazing --

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.801
We had the most
amazing production design

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.868
and we had
the most incredible crew.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.167
And they just got me
those tiny little forks.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:56.968
-Yeah.
-And tiny little wine bottle.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.734
-A little, tiny wine bottle.
-It was just incredible.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:03.234
-It's so well-done,
and you cast some great people

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.300
in here to play --

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.100
-Oh, yeah,
I was really lucky with

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.267
the casting of
my beautiful children.

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:11.133
-Mary Elizabeth Ellis,
John Early,

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:14.033
and, of course,
Mike Birbiglia, right there,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.267
who is one of the funniest
human beings I know.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.467
-Absolutely.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.167
-And you were saying
that I might have had

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.667
something to do with
him getting cast?

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:25.901
-Well, so, I --
One of the prerequisites

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:31.100
of when I cast anyone for
anything is like, "Are they fun?

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.367
And are they nice?

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.033
And are we gonna have
a fun time on set?"

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.400
Obviously, like, talent --
that's number one,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.801
like, "Do you fit the part?"

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:40.434
But then there's also
this sort of caveat of like,

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.200
"Well, like, we're gonna be on
set for a while.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.000
Like, is this gonna be a blast
or is this --

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.300
You know, does this person
have, like,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.033
this internal struggle
with what they do

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.767
and they can't stand acting,
but they're good at it?

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.167
Like, it's -- I meet a lot of
people out and about,

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.801
and that's how I'll cast things.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:57.734
So, you had a pizza party,
and I went to it.

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:59.567
And I ended up
in a corner talking to

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:03.033
Mike Birbiglia and his wife,
Jen, who's a poet, all night.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.701
They're the most
wonderful people.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.934
And I just remember thinking --
'Cause I'd seen Mike in things

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.534
and I'd seen some of his --

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.100
You know,
he does these amazing shows.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.000
He just makes such thoughtful
performances and comedy.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.501
-He has a new one
coming out on Broadway.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.267
-Yeah, he has one
that I can't wait to see.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.701
-Yeah.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:21.534
-And, so, I was talking to them
and I was just thinking --

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.133
I'd written the
"Anti-Hero" video.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:25.200
And I was like, "He's perfect.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.734
I want him to play my son
Preston."

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:30.000
My future son.
-Yeah, future son Preston.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.601
-My country-club-going son,
Preston.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.601
-And they get in
a big argument over the will

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:34.667
and what you left them.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.734
-Yeah, it was great.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:40.000
Like, I also met
Mary Elizabeth Ellis at a party.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.534
And, so, that's --
It's a great way to...

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:44.000
-Cast.
-...to cast stuff.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.701
-Just go to parties.

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:48.033
-You don't -- You know,
nobody has to audition.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:49.501
Just come up
and say hi at a party.

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:52.100
-We had amazing pizza
that night.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.400
And then --
-It was great. It was a blast.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.734
I mean, there's some good
pictures from that night, too.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.901
-Well, you had this camera.
You had a really cool camera.

00:03:58.901 --> 00:03:59.968
I don't know -- it was, like,

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.200
something from
the '80s or something.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.467
-Push the button,
it goes flash.

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:03.968
-Yeah, and it's real film.
-Then you remember it.

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:06.534
-And, so, there's a nice photo
that I really appreciate you --

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:07.968
I don't know how this happened.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.234
But at one point, we ended up
doing a cheerleader pyramid.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.534
-That's -- Yeah.
That's because --

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.400
-That's me there.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.467
-Yeah.
That's because wine, as well.

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.167
-Yeah, wine.
Wine was involved, yeah.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.701
-That's --
-And there's Mike.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:20.734
And there's Jack.

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:22.968
And then I thought
it'd be funny --

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.534
'Cause we were having fun.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.701
And there was other people
on this side, too.

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:28.067
And I was taking your camera

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.534
and I just I kept
taking photos of other things.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:30.901
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:32.767
Which everybody loves that guy.
You know what I mean?

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:34.801
'Cause then you go
and you get the candid shots.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.968
And then I develop the pictures.
I'm like, "That's so great.

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.334
I didn't know that happened."

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:40.467
-Yeah. And then you're in
some of the photos,

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:41.601
'cause it usually --
If it's your camera,

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:42.667
you're taking all the pictures.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.300
-Yeah, it's a good guy to be.
-Yeah.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.601
And then I took probably
the worst photo

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:50.167
I've ever seen of myself ever.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:51.968
-Let's see it.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:55.133
-I'm gonna show it because --
but I'm upset to really show it.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.434
I'm not -- know
if I'm ready for this.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.501
But Jack keeps
sending this to me

00:04:58.501 --> 00:04:59.868
because he thinks
it's the funniest thing.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:01.400
It's so bad.
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.467
Honestly, this is,
like, therapeutic for me.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:07.667
Alright, here it is,
a selfie that I took of myself.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.100
[ Sad tuba plays, cymbal crash ]

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.033
-Wow.
[ Laughs ]

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.267
-What -- It's so gross.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.100
-It's so beautiful.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.234
-It looks like I have
tape on my nose.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:24.100
-I just never thought
I'd see inside of your brain.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.767
It's so special to get to see
all the way up the nostril,

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:30.334
into the nasal cavities.

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.067
-It's the worst thing
I've ever seen.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:35.033
And I go, "I have to just --
I have to lay it all out there."

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:37.334
Like, I'm taking lessons
from you from "Midnights."

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:39.501
I'm laying it all out there.
-That's a gorgeous photo.

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:41.434
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:44.100
Because that's what
the night really was.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.300
Okay?
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.701
-Pyramid, everybody's posing.
-This I love.

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:52.534
-This was the mode
I was in that night.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.834
This is the goal I'm trying --
-Whew!

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:56.334
And you can't delete film.

00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:58.367
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:00.734
That is the most embarrassing --
I'm sweating.

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.501
Can you feel the heat
coming off of me?

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:04.934
It's so bad.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:06.801
You've announced
that a new video

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:07.868
is coming out
at midnight tonight.

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:11.501
-Yes, yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:13.634
-It's around midnight.

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:14.868
It's around midnight right now.

00:06:14.868 --> 00:06:17.367
Can you say what song
this video is for?

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:19.501
-It's for a song called
"Bejeweled."

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:22.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.334
Oh, good.
-Love it.

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:25.667
-They approve.
-Yes.

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:28.000
-Okay, so, basically,
the first video, "Anti-Hero,"

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.868
I was like, "This is
gonna be the first single."

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:32.000
And I knew that.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.234
But I was like,
"I want to make a video

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:37.934
that is just for the fans
who like certain things,

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:44.634
like glitter and Easter eggs and
lots of little cameos."

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.067
And, so, basically,

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:47.934
I was thinking about
"Midnights," the concept

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:50.200
and I was like, "Where do we
hear about midnights a lot?"

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.367
We hear about it a lot

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:54.801
when we talk about
the Cinderella fairy tale.

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:56.133
And so I was like,

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:59.300
"What if we did a little twist
on a Cinderella story?

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.501
And I could cast my friends."

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:04.133
You know, like, my best friends,
the Haim sisters --

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.501
what if they played
the step-sisters?

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:08.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.734 --> 00:07:12.601
And I was like, "What if
we really shoot for the stars

00:07:12.601 --> 00:07:14.000
with the other casting,
with, like --

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.400
You know, what if it was, like,

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:19.801
Oscar winner Laura Dern playing
my step-mother?"

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:22.501
-How'd you get in touch with
Laura Dern?

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:24.400
-It was like,
"Oscar winner Laura Dern..."

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.200
-Yes.
-"...hello.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.467
Um, I've written a script.

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:33.334
It's a one-scene script in
which you are going to call me

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:35.734
a "tired, tacky wench."

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:38.701
-And she was like, "I'm in."
-And she was like, "I'm down."

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.501
She's the coolest.
She's so funny.

00:07:40.501 --> 00:07:43.334
She's another one.
I'm like, "Friend."

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:45.868
-Yes.
-"You are my friend now."

00:07:45.868 --> 00:07:48.767
-How do you direct Laura Dern,
Oscar winner Laura Dern?

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:52.634
-Oh, I mean, you know, directing
Oscar winner Laura Dern

00:07:52.634 --> 00:07:54.801
is easier than anything
I've ever done in my life.

00:07:54.801 --> 00:07:57.334
-Yeah, just she just goes,
"I know how to do it, yeah."

00:07:57.334 --> 00:07:59.434
-Well, yeah, I mean,
she's just the greatest.

00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:02.200
And she's -- I mean, I don't --

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.067
I don't even believe
I'm saying things like this.

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:07.167
-And then -- And so, then,
we have one of

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:08.501
my favorite performers,
who I think

00:08:08.501 --> 00:08:11.834
has been so influential
in pop music.

00:08:11.834 --> 00:08:14.534
And I've nicknamed
this character

00:08:14.534 --> 00:08:16.467
not the Fairy Godmother,
but the Fairy Goddess,

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:18.834
and that is played by
Dita Von Teese,

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:22.734
who is, I think, one of the most
iconic performers.

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:24.767
And it's so exciting
to get to see her

00:08:24.767 --> 00:08:25.901
do what she does in this.

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:30.200
-Yes.
-Jack Antonoff is in it.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:34.200
The genius, legendary
make-up artist

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.501
and creator Pat McGrath
is in it.

00:08:36.501 --> 00:08:38.000
-Oh, yeah.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.501
-So, I'm really,
really, really excited.

00:08:39.501 --> 00:08:43.801
-And this one, you were saying,
but I will let you say again.

00:08:43.801 --> 00:08:45.501
This has maybe
the most Easter eggs.

00:08:45.501 --> 00:08:47.467
-A psychotic amount.

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:51.934
It is like --
We have a PDF file

00:08:51.934 --> 00:08:53.934
for the Easter eggs
in this video.

00:08:53.934 --> 00:08:55.868
-Yes!

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:59.434
-Because there are so many that
we could not keep track.

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:01.634
-Oh, I love it. Alright.

00:09:01.634 --> 00:09:02.968
Everyone, check it out right now

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:04.400
and see how many
Easter eggs you can find.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.634
We love it
every time you are here.

00:09:05.634 --> 00:09:07.133
You hit a home run
with this one, buddy.

00:09:07.133 --> 00:09:08.734
-Thank you so much!

00:09:08.734 --> 00:09:10.534
-A home run.

00:09:10.534 --> 00:09:12.501
We love you.
Taylor Swift, everybody.

00:09:12.501 --> 00:09:15.000
The new album,
"Midnights," is out now.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.067
Meghan Trainor joins us
after the break.

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:18.300
Stick around!

